surrounded by a lot of bugs.

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,880
John starts
exploring a solution.

5
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,600
He surfs through the internet,
checks programmer communities.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,210
Doubting every step
of the way, John

7
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:21,180
feels his problem is not solved.

8
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:25,680
Desperate to find the solution,
John meets his friend Adam.

9
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,110
Adam comes up with an
idea of an artificially

10
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:33,060
intelligent and practical
solution called the ChatGPT.

11
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:35,490
Adam says ChatGPT
has the caliber

12
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,830
to systematically
resolve all the bugs

13
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:41,340
with an elaborate explanation
for every step it makes.

14
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:44,010
ChatGPT is an
AI-trained model that

15
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:48,480
works in a conversational
way, developed by OpenAI.

16
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:51,390
Fascinated by hearing
this, John asks

17
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:53,290
Adam to explain him in detail.

18
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:57,120
After Adam explains
that, GPT a.k.a.

19
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:59,430
generative pre-training
transformer,

20
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,210
has come a long way.

21
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:05,230
Before the introduction of GPT,
natural language processing

22
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:09,250
used to deal with a specific
task with large amounts of data.

23
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:13,240
GPT was first released
in 2018, which contained

24
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:16,270
117 million parameters.

25
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:21,400
GPT, GPT-2, and GPT-3,
each one is stronger

26
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,050
than the one before it.

27
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:26,380
The main reason why GPT
received little attention

28
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:30,220
was that it was more of an idea
or test than a finished product.

29
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,890
But after the
introduction of GPT-2,

30
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:35,620
it gained a lot of attention,
as it could accurately

31
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,110
predict the word that
would begin a text.

32
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:42,400
Then they introduced GPT-3,
which is a strong language

33
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,580
model, achieving translation,
question-answering,

34
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:48,360
and performing
three-digit arithmetic.

35
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:52,260
But ChatGPT stands tall compared
to all other achievements

36
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,240
of OpenAI.

37
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,180
So how does it work?

38
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:57,810
ChatGPT uses deep
learning techniques

39
00:01:57,810 --> 00:01:59,950
to generate human-like text.

40
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:01,440
It is based on the
machine learning

41
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:04,380
model derived from the class
called, the large language

42
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:05,250
model.

43
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:09,150
ChatGPT is a byproduct
of InstructGPT.

44
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:11,520
InstructGPT
introduced a strategy

45
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:14,550
for integrating human feedback
into the training process

46
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,560
to match model outputs.

47
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:21,210
This innovative technology
made ChatGPT exceptional.

48
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:23,880
It is trained on the
massive data sets of text

49
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,890
from the internet and
learns from the patterns

50
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:28,570
and relationships between
words and phrases.

51
00:02:28,570 --> 00:02:31,800
It responds to a prompt by
determining the next word based

52
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,560
on the context, then
repeats the process

53
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,870
until a stop condition is met.

54
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:41,130
As a result, ChatGPT can produce
various logical responses

55
00:02:41,130 --> 00:02:43,260
to various queries and prompts.

56
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:46,170
The most important
components of ChatGPT

57
00:02:46,170 --> 00:02:49,450
are the transformer
model and language model.

58
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:51,700
Coming to the
transformer model, it

59
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,980
is a neural network
architecture designed

60
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,020
to process sequential data.

61
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:58,870
It consists of multiple
layers of self-attention

62
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:01,420
and a feedforward network.

63
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:04,540
After the transformer model
has processed the input,

64
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,820
a decoder generates the output.

65
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:10,210
The decoder uses the context
provided by the encoder

66
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:12,100
to generate the response.

67
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,950
The model is trained using
unsupervised learning

68
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:19,300
and fine-tuned on specific
tasks using supervised learning.

69
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,430
For successful
completion of tasks,

70
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:23,800
it needs pre-trained data.

71
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:26,440
The model first
encodes the input text,

72
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:29,150
then converts it to a
numerical representation,

73
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:32,140
which can be processed by
the model's neural network.

74
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:35,020
This encoding is done using
the embedded layer that

75
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,430
maps the work.

76
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:38,650
Then comes the language model.

77
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:41,980
ChatGPT is trained as a
language model, trained

78
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:44,080
to predict the next
word in a sequence given

79
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,580
the previous words.

80
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:48,970
The language model intends to
produce rational, consistent.

81
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:50,800
And meaningful output.

82
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:55,240
The pre-trained ChatGPT can
be tuned for a specific task.

83
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:58,150
So ChatGPT passes
a fine-tuning test

84
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:01,150
by answering questions,
generating text summaries,

85
00:04:01,150 --> 00:04:04,300
or generating text in
response to a query.

86
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:07,750
Overall, ChatGPT is a
powerful language model

87
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,310
with a combination
of techniques.

88
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:12,100
Like deep learning, machine
learning, neural networks,

89
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,590
and natural language processing.

90
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:17,079
Can ChatGPT change
a wide variety

91
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,510
of business tasks, John asked?

92
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:23,410
ChatGPT possesses the ability
to automate content creation

93
00:04:23,410 --> 00:04:27,100
on social media, create
chatbot and e-commerce sites,

94
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:30,400
provide medical assistance by
acting as a symptom checker,

95
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:33,400
write code and
assist a developer.

96
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:37,570
Thus, ChatGPT can change the
working of every industry.

97
00:04:37,570 --> 00:04:39,970
Now, John can resolve
any coding issue

98
00:04:39,970 --> 00:04:42,700
without looking into
any other resources.

99
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:45,850
But like any other
technology, ChatGPT

100
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:49,690
comes with a few limitations
that can be its Achilles heel.

101
00:04:49,690 --> 00:04:54,160
ChatGPT is capable of
developing content up to 2021.

102
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,920
It finds difficulty in
providing logical reasoning

103
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,540
in certain situations.

104
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:02,530
And also, ChatGPT lags in
translation, summarization,

105
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:05,020
and sometimes
question-answering.

106
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:09,280
But above all, ChatGPT has
shown remarkable ability

107
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:13,030
by providing accurate answers
flawlessly in a creative way

108
00:05:13,030 --> 00:05:15,730
in very short periods of time.

109
